  "notes": "# What\u2019s new in OverCue Desktop 2.1.8 for Windows\n\n- Tracks no longer fail with \u201cwaveform time axis differs from the template\u201d when rekordbox\u2019s own waveform data disagrees by a few points.\n- AIFF files whose header overstates their size, as some tag editors leave them, now process normally. Files with audio that is actually cut short are still refused.\n- When a USB\u2019s stem list is full, OverCue now stops before processing each new track and explains how to make room, instead of failing after separation.\n",
